    "https://jobs.wisc.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-or-full-professor-tenured-or-tenure-track-madison-wisconsin-united-states-1ff4bcd0-228f-45b7-89fe-81b232fd7953": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate or Full Professor (Tenured or Tenure Track)",
      "description": "Assistant, Associate or Full Professor (Tenured or Tenure Track) - Madison, Wisconsin, United States Assistant, Associate or Full Professor (Tenured or Tenure Track) - Madison, Wisconsin, United States Skip to main content Kiosk mode Assistant, Associate or Full Professor (Tenured or Tenure Track) Requisition Number: JR10014927 Remote Type: On Site Location: Madison, Wisconsin Category: Faculty Time Type: Full time Current Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Jobs Hub to apply through the internal application process. Job Category: Faculty Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Professor Job Summary: The Department of Biochemistry ( https://biochem.wisc.edu/ ) at the University of Wisconsin–Madison invites applications for a full-time, 9-month, faculty position. We are particularly interested in candidates with expertise in solid state nuclear magnetic resonance (ssNMR) and its application to biological systems or development of new NMR methods and technology. We welcome candidates committed to democratizing access to NMR through community engagement, outreach, and training in the tradition of the National Magnetic Resonance Facility at Madison (NMRFAM). The successful candidate will join a strong and collaborative department with broad and complementary strengths across the biochemical sciences. Current research areas include structural biology, virology, metabolism, gene regulation, cell and molecular biology, chemical biology, biophysics, systems biology, synthetic biology and computational biology. The department fosters a highly interactive environment, with a culture of collaboration and intellectual exchange that supports interdisciplinary research and innovation. The scientific environment at UW–Madison provides exceptional opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration across the biological sciences, engineering, and data science. Faculty benefit from access to state-of-the-art facilities and centers, including the NMRFAM, the UW-Madison Cryo-EM Research Center, and many other advanced resources that support all aspects of biochemistry. The university’s collaborative culture and strong cross-disciplinary programs create a uniquely supportive setting for developing innovative and impactful research programs. The position is an academic (9-month) tenure-track (junior) or tenured (mid-career or senior) faculty position. The successful applicant will be expected to establish an ambitious, externally funded research program and contribute to our core missions of undergraduate and graduate teaching and service. Key Job Responsibilities: Developing and directing a well-recognized and extramurally funded research program; working collaboratively to develop NMRFAM technology, user outreach and training programs; teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses and contributing to curriculum updates and innovations to educate a diverse student body; mentoring graduate students and supervising their research; participating in departmental and university faculty governance; contributing to professional and public service, and participating in interdisciplinary and collaborative efforts with other departments, schools, and colleges. Department: Department of Biochemistry, College of Agricultural and Life Sciences ( https://biochem.wisc.edu/ ) Work Type: Faculty Full Time: 100% Location: Madison, Wisconsin It is anticipated this position requires work be performed in-person, onsite, in HF DeLuca Biochemistry Laboratories. Appointment Type, Duration: Ongoing (tenured)/Renewable (tenure-track) Anticipated Begin Date: AUGUST 23, 2027 (first day of academic year), but this is negotiable. Compensation: Negotiable - ACADEMIC (9 months) Required Qualifications: The successful candidate will have an excellent academic record, a vision for an innovative and impactful research program, the skills to implement it, and a commitment to high quality and inclusive undergraduate and graduate instruction and mentoring. Applicants at any rank are encouraged to apply. At the rank of Associate or (full) Professor the selected candidate's qualifications must be sufficient to meet the requirements for tenure in the Department of Biochemistry, in the College of Agricultural and Life Sciences at the University of Wisconsin-Madison by the position start date. All requirements must be met by position start date Preferred Qualifications: Education: Required: PhD in biochemistry or a relevant biological science, physical science, or engineering discipline. Additional Information: NMRFAM has a 40 year history of being at the forefront of biological NMR research in the US. NMRFAM is dedicated to making cutting-edge NMR instruments and methods available to all scientists; to developing new NMR instrumentation, methods and data analysis; and to making NMR accessible to biological science researchers without significant NMR expertise. This mission, namely to make the technology, data analysis, and training available to UW-Madison faculty, staff and students, and researchers from the state of Wisconsin and across the United States, strives to embody the Wisconsin Idea in a format appropriate for this highly advanced technology. NMRFAM has been very successful in obtaining large NIH and NSF grants for both user program support and technology development. Faculty associated with NMRFAM are expected to contribute to development of new technology, user outreach, and our training mission. Significant investments by the Biochemistry Department, CALS, and our recent NSF award for the 1.1 GHz NMR have greatly increased the solid-state NMR capabilities of NMRFAM. The ideal candidate would have a research focus in this area to make best use of the available instrumentation. They will collaborate with other NMRFAM faculty and staff to lead NMRFAM technology development, keep NMRFAM at the forefront of the field, attract top staff and students, and lead the US biological NMR community. How to Apply: Applicants will be asked to upload a single .pdf file comprising of: a cover letter highlighting your relevant training, skills, or experience including any expertise in solid state NMR and its application, or development of new NMR methods and technology, a 2-page statement of research, a 1-page teaching interests, and a curriculum vitae. Applicants must also provide contact information for three references within the application. The deadline for assuring full consideration is October 30th, 2026; however, positions may remain open and applications may be considered until all positions are filled. Contact Information: For questions about position details please contact: Katherine Henzler-Wildman - Professor - henzlerwildm@wisc.edu For questions about application status/updates, or technical assistance please contact: Megan Sullivan - Human Resources - megan.sullivan@wisc.edu Institutional Statement on Diversity: Diversity is a source of strength, creativity, and innovation for UW-Madison. We value the contributions of each person and respect the profound ways their identity, culture, background, experience, status, abilities, and opinion enrich the university community. We commit ourselves to the pursuit of excellence in teaching, research, outreach, and diversity as inextricably linked goals. The University of Wisconsin-Madison fulfills its public mission by creating a welcoming and inclusive community for people from every background - people who as students, faculty, and staff serve Wisconsin and the world. The University of Wisconsin-Madison is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to, including but not limited to, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, or status as a protected veteran and other bases as defined by federal regulations and UW System policies. We promote excellence by acknowledging skills and expertise from all backgrounds and encourage all qualified individuals to apply. For more information regarding applicant and employee rights and to view federal and state required postings, visit the Human Resources Workplace Poster website . To request a disability or pregnancy-related accommodation for any step in the hiring process (e.g., application, interview, pre-employment testing, etc.), please contact the Divisional Disability Representative (DDR) in the division you are applying to. Please make your request as soon as possible to help the university respond most effectively to you. Employment may require a criminal background check. It may also require your references to answer questions regarding misconduct, including sexual violence and sexual harassment. The University of Wisconsin System will not reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing, except that the identity of the successful candidate will be released. See Wis. Stat. sec. 19.36(7). The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains current campus safety and disciplinary policies, crime statistics for the previous 3 calendar years, and on-campus student housing fire safety policies and fire statistics for the previous 3 calendar years. UW-Madison will provide a paper copy upon request; please contact the University of Wisconsin Police Department . Apply Now Are you a current employee at any University of Wisconsin campus? I am a current employee I am not a current employee Log in to Jobs Hub to apply: Please search for requisition JR10014927 in Workday Jobs Hub to get started. Log in to Workday Please enter your information below: First Name (required) 5f93c473 Last Name (required) 4ab2d615 Email address (required) 87ea52d5 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? You will be redirected to the application to launch your career momentarily. Thank you! Questions? Frequently Asked Questions Disability Accommodations Pay Transparency Policy Statement Contact Us Refer a Friend Your First Name (required) 71e56da6 Your Last Name (required) fbe6bcb4 Your Email Address (required) 92e21e7e Friend's Information: bcffc1c6 Send Please wait... Done Not You? You've sent this job to a friend! Website feedback, questions or accessibility issues: ohrwebmaster@ohr.wisc.edu . Learn more about accessibility at UW–Madison . © 2016–2026 Board of Regents of the University of Wisconsin System • Privacy Statement Before You Go.. Would You Like To Sign-up For Job Alerts? First Name (required) 2a7453e6 Last Name (required) 4288e505 Email address (required) 12948142 Job Alert Subscription d1b41e73 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Full time Full time Subscribe Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for subscribing to UW–Madison job alerts! Close Candidate Details We use cookies on this site. By continuing to browse without changing your browser settings to block or delete cookies, you agree to the UW–Madison Privacy Notice . I do not accept I accept Please choose the employment type(s)"
